
=== a request parses as a watch only when it asks to wait
a plain get is still a get: ok
one that asks to wait carries the deadline and the token: ok
a wait longer than this end allows is cut down to it: ok
holding costs no storage slot: ok
and it is still authorised against its own key: ok

=== a client that is already behind is answered, never held
a client with no token at all is answered: ok
answered at once rather than held to the deadline: ok
and it says this end understood the wait: ok
one read to decide it: ok

=== a client that is up to date is held until the deadline
no content, the deadline having passed: ok
still marked as understood: ok
and the store was not asked again while it was held: ok

=== many waiters on one key cost the store one read per change
every waiter was answered: ok
  waiters: 8, store reads: 9
one read per arrival, and one for the change: ok
